    "created_at": "2021-11-30T16:07:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-30T16:07:58Z",
    "body": "That's a good question. I don't know. I think it makes sense for it to return false in that case since we haven't \"allocated\" visual space for the image. \r\n\r\nI'm also weary about exposing too much internal optimizations for no good reason. For example, for `<iframe>`s, I propose that this returns true even if the UA decided to throttle the frame for whatever reason. \r\n\r\nI'm also actually a bit on the fence about `content-visibility: auto` elements -- maybe it should just return true",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
